# Ring-closure bookkeeping. The digit is a *label*, not an identity: it is
# freed the moment its pair closes and may be reused immediately, which is the
# rule naive implementations get wrong.

C1CCCCC1 cyclohexane
# Two independent rings reusing digit 1 — legal, and a parser that treats
# digits as globally unique mis-bonds it.
C1CCCCC1C1CCCCC1 bicyclohexyl
# Fused, sharing an edge.
c1ccc2ccccc2c1 naphthalene
# Bridged: three closures open before any of them shut.
C1CC2CCC1C2 norbornane
# Past nine, where the two-digit %NN form becomes mandatory.
C%10CCCCC%10 cyclohexane-high-label
# A closure carrying an explicit bond order. Cyclopentadiene rather than
# benzene so this does not duplicate aromatics.smi, where the Kekule/aromatic
# pair is the point rather than an accident.
C1=CC=CC1 kekule-cyclopentadiene
